# Response headers for the Cloudflare deploy (Workers static assets read
# this file). The local dev server (tools/serve.py) sends them too, except
# Cache-Control, so the Content-Security-Policy is exercised while developing.
#
# no-cache means "check with the server before using a stored copy", so an
# edited app.js reaches the tablets on their next load, as with `just serve`.
# The microphone is allowed for this site only; recording needs it. So is
# display-capture: 🎧 From a song listens to another tab or the screen.
#
# The policy allows exactly what the page loads: its own scripts and styles,
# its own fonts (web/fonts/), blob: URLs for downloads and data: for the tab
# icon. One outside origin: Cloudflare's Web Analytics beacon, which Cloudflare
# adds at the edge and which reports page views to cloudflareinsights.com (Ben,
# 2026-10-20). No inline script or style, no framing, no plugins.
# Adding a new origin or inline code means changing this line on purpose.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Permissions-Policy: microphone=(self), display-capture=(self), accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; connect-src 'self' https://cloudflareinsights.com; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
